# NEX Climate Data Extraction

Purpose: prepare projected weather for Agronaut.

Demo location: London, Ontario — 43.0, -81.25.
Future period: 2041–2060.
Scenario: SSP2-4.5.
Models: ACCESS-CM2, MPI-ESM1-2-HR, MRI-ESM2-0.

Variables:
- Daily minimum temperature, converted to Celsius.
- Daily maximum temperature, converted to Celsius.
- Daily precipitation, converted to mm/day.

Script: backend/data_scripts/extract_nex.py
Output: backend/data/nex/london_demo.json

Data source:
https://ds.nccs.nasa.gov/thredds/catalog/AMES/NEX/GDDP-CMIP6/catalog.html

Keep each climate model separate.
Label results as projected climate, not observed weather.

Current MVP future period: 2031–2050. The London 2041–2060 demo described above
is retained as an earlier extraction artifact; it is not relabeled for the MVP.
Use extract_nex_region.py --future 2031 2050 for regional model-specific change
factors against matched 1995–2014 model reference years. The corrected engine
uses matched POWER reference daily sequences and independently simulates every
model, then summarizes outcomes. See SCIENTIFIC_VALIDITY.md for the explicit
mean-temperature/DTR method, event-sequence limitations and frontend contract.
